IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `coa-core`

-- coa24-language.l4: Part 35 "Language requirements: translation" and "Language requirements: transliteration", ss 1102
-- to 1110 of the Companies Act 2006 (lines 15807-15872 of ukpga-2006-46.txt). Layer 1: the law, objectively.
--
-- WHAT IS NOT ENCODED. ss 1102(2), (4), 1105(3), 1106(2), (5), 1108(2)-(3) and 1110 are powers of the Secretary of
-- State to make regulations: machinery, inert (reason 2) in NOTES.md. What the regulations say (which documents are
-- excepted from translation, which characters are permitted, which languages the voluntary facility covers) is not in the
-- sources: it comes in as an input and a NOTHING input passes through as NOTHING.
--
-- HOW TO READ AN ANSWER (the rule of 2026-10-29; assumed, not ruled by a lawyer). MAYBE answers: JUST TRUE is the text
-- saying yes; JUST FALSE is the text saying no in its own words (each such branch carries
-- `-- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "<words>"`); NOTHING is "not covered" (each NOTHING branch says why,
-- as `-- NOTHING-kind (<why>)`). A function whose name ends "meets the requirement of s N" answers JUST FALSE when the
-- "must" it cites is not done: that is a fork line in NOTES.md, not a ruling.

§ `Part 35: language requirements (ss 1102 to 1110)`

-- ---- s 1102 ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:15809 | (1) The provisions listed below apply to all documents required to be delivered to the registrar under any provision of—
-- src:15810 | (a) the Companies Acts, or
-- src:15811 | (b) the Insolvency Act 1986 (c. 45) or the Insolvency (Northern Ireland) Order 1989 (S.I. 1989/2405 (N.I. 19)).
@ref s 1102(1) The listed provisions apply to all documents required to be delivered to the registrar (src:15809-15811)
GIVEN `the document is required to be delivered to the registrar under a provision of the Companies Acts` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the document is required to be delivered to the registrar under a provision of the Insolvency Act 1986 or the Insolvency (Northern Ireland) Order 1989` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1102(1) the language provisions apply to the document` MEANS
    IF `the document is required to be delivered to the registrar under a provision of the Companies Acts` OR `the document is required to be delivered to the registrar under a provision of the Insolvency Act 1986 or the Insolvency (Northern Ireland) Order 1989`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): subsection (2) lets the Secretary of State apply the provisions by regulations to documents delivered under any other enactment

-- src:15813 | (3) The provisions are—
-- src:15814 | section 1103 (documents to be drawn up and delivered in English),
-- src:15815 | section 1104 (documents relating to Welsh companies),
-- src:15816 | section 1105 (documents that may be drawn up and delivered in other languages),
-- src:15817 | section 1107 (certified translations).
@ref s 1102(3) The provisions that apply (src:15813-15817)
`s 1102(3) the provisions that apply under subsection (1)` MEANS LIST
    "section 1103 (documents to be drawn up and delivered in English)"
    "section 1104 (documents relating to Welsh companies)"
    "section 1105 (documents that may be drawn up and delivered in other languages)"
    "section 1107 (certified translations)"

-- ---- s 1103 ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:15820 | (1) The general rule is that all documents required to be delivered to the registrar must be drawn up and delivered in English.
-- src:15821 | (2) This is subject to—
-- src:15822 | section 1104 (documents relating to Welsh companies) and
-- src:15823 | section 1105 (documents that may be drawn up and delivered in other languages).
@ref s 1103 Documents to be drawn up and delivered in English (src:15820-15823)
GIVEN `s 1104(1) the document may be drawn up and delivered in Welsh` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 1105(1) the document may be drawn up and delivered in a language other than English` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1103 the document must be drawn up and delivered in English` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 1104(1) the document may be drawn up and delivered in Welsh`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This is subject to— section 1104 (documents relating to Welsh companies) and section 1105"
    OTHERWISE
        CONSIDER `s 1105(1) the document may be drawn up and delivered in a language other than English`
        WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This is subject to— ... section 1105 (documents that may be drawn up and delivered in other languages)"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE -- no exception of section 1104 or 1105 is made out, so the general rule stands: "all documents required to be delivered to the registrar must be drawn up and delivered in English"

-- ---- s 1104 ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:15825 | (1) Documents relating to a Welsh company may be drawn up and delivered to the registrar in Welsh.
@ref s 1104(1) Documents relating to a Welsh company may be delivered in Welsh (src:15825)
GIVEN `s 88 the company is a Welsh company` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1104(1) the document may be drawn up and delivered in Welsh` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 88 the company is a Welsh company`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Documents relating to a Welsh company may be drawn up and delivered to the registrar in Welsh" grants the case of a Welsh company and does not forbid Welsh for other companies
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the company is a Welsh company is defined by section 88, which is not in this part

-- src:15826 | (2) On delivery to the registrar any such document must be accompanied by a certified translation into English, unless it is—
-- src:15827 | (a) of a description excepted from that requirement by regulations made by the Secretary of State, or
-- src:15828 | (b) in a form prescribed in Welsh (or partly in Welsh and partly in English) by virtue of section 26 of the Welsh Language Act 1993 (c. 38).
@ref s 1104(2) A document delivered in Welsh must be accompanied by a certified translation into English unless excepted (src:15826-15828)
GIVEN `the document relating to a Welsh company is delivered in Welsh` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the document is of a description excepted from that requirement by regulations made by the Secretary of State` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the document is in a form prescribed in Welsh (or partly in Welsh and partly in English) by virtue of section 26 of the Welsh Language Act 1993` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1104(2) the document must be accompanied by a certified translation into English` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the document relating to a Welsh company is delivered in Welsh`)
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "On delivery to the registrar any such document", that is a document relating to a Welsh company drawn up and delivered in Welsh
    ELSE IF `the document is in a form prescribed in Welsh (or partly in Welsh and partly in English) by virtue of section 26 of the Welsh Language Act 1993`
         THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless it is— ... (b) in a form prescribed in Welsh (or partly in Welsh and partly in English) by virtue of section 26 of the Welsh Language Act 1993"
         ELSE CONSIDER `the document is of a description excepted from that requirement by regulations made by the Secretary of State`
              WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless it is— (a) of a description excepted from that requirement by regulations made by the Secretary of State"
              WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST TRUE
              WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the descriptions excepted by regulations are not in the sources

@ref s 1104(2) The delivery meets the requirement (src:15826-15828)
GIVEN `the document relating to a Welsh company is delivered in Welsh` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the document is of a description excepted from that requirement by regulations made by the Secretary of State` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the document is in a form prescribed in Welsh (or partly in Welsh and partly in English) by virtue of section 26 of the Welsh Language Act 1993` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the document is accompanied by a certified translation into English` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1104(2) the delivery meets the requirement of s 1104(2)` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 1104(2) the document must be accompanied by a certified translation into English` `the document relating to a Welsh company is delivered in Welsh` `the document is of a description excepted from that requirement by regulations made by the Secretary of State` `the document is in a form prescribed in Welsh (or partly in Welsh and partly in English) by virtue of section 26 of the Welsh Language Act 1993`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
        IF `the document is accompanied by a certified translation into English`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "On delivery to the registrar any such document must be accompanied by a certified translation into English"
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the document is excepted by regulations is not in the sources

-- src:15829 | (3) Where a document is properly delivered to the registrar in Welsh without a certified translation into English, the registrar must obtain such a translation if the document is to be available for public inspection.
-- src:15830 | The translation is treated as if delivered to the registrar in accordance with the same provision as the original.
@ref s 1104(3) The registrar must obtain a translation if the document is to be available for public inspection (src:15829-15830)
GIVEN `the document is properly delivered to the registrar in Welsh without a certified translation into English` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the document is to be available for public inspection` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1104(3) the registrar must obtain a translation into English` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the document is properly delivered to the registrar in Welsh without a certified translation into English`)
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a document is properly delivered to the registrar in Welsh without a certified translation into English, the registrar must obtain such a translation"
    ELSE IF `the document is to be available for public inspection`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the registrar must obtain such a translation if the document is to be available for public inspection"

@ref s 1104(3) The translation is treated as delivered under the same provision as the original (src:15830)
GIVEN `the registrar has obtained a translation under this subsection` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1104(3) the translation is treated as delivered in accordance with the same provision as the original` MEANS
    IF `the registrar has obtained a translation under this subsection`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The translation" is the one the registrar must obtain under this subsection

-- src:15831 | (4) A Welsh company may deliver to the registrar a certified translation into Welsh of any document in English that relates to the company and is or has been delivered to the registrar.
@ref s 1104(4) A Welsh company may deliver a certified translation into Welsh of an English document (src:15831)
GIVEN `s 88 the company is a Welsh company` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the document is in English, relates to the company and is or has been delivered to the registrar` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1104(4) the company may deliver a certified translation into Welsh of the document` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 88 the company is a Welsh company`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
        IF `the document is in English, relates to the company and is or has been delivered to the registrar`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any document in English that relates to the company and is or has been delivered to the registrar"
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A Welsh company may deliver" grants a Welsh company the power and does not deny it to others
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the company is a Welsh company is defined by section 88, which is not in this part

-- src:15832 | (5) Section 1105 (which requires certified translations into English of documents delivered to the registrar in another language) does not apply to a document relating to a Welsh company that is drawn up and delivered in Welsh.
@ref s 1104(5) Section 1105 does not apply to a Welsh company's document drawn up and delivered in Welsh (src:15832)
GIVEN `s 88 the company is a Welsh company` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the document relates to the company and is drawn up and delivered in Welsh` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1104(5) section 1105 applies to the document` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 88 the company is a Welsh company`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
        IF `the document relates to the company and is drawn up and delivered in Welsh`
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Section 1105 ... does not apply to a document relating to a Welsh company that is drawn up and delivered in Welsh"
        ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the exclusion covers only a document drawn up and delivered in Welsh
    OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the exclusion covers only a document relating to a Welsh company

-- ---- s 1105 ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

DECLARE `s 1105(2) description of document` IS ONE OF
    `s 1105(2)(a) an agreement required to be forwarded to the registrar under Chapter 3 of Part 3 (agreements affecting the company's constitution)`
    `s 1105(2)(b) a document required to be delivered under section 400(2)(e) or section 401(2)(f) (company included in accounts of larger group: copy of group accounts)`
    `s 1105(2)(c) a certified copy delivered under Part 25 (company charges)`
    `s 1105(2)(d) a document of any other description specified in regulations made by the Secretary of State`
    `s 1105(2) another document`

-- src:15835 | (2) This section applies to—
-- src:15836 | (a) agreements required to be forwarded to the registrar under Chapter 3 of Part 3 (agreements affecting the company's constitution);
-- src:15837 | (b) documents required to be delivered under section 400(2)(e) or section 401(2)(f) (company included in accounts of larger group: required to deliver copy of group accounts);
-- src:15838 | (c) certified copies delivered under Part 25 (company charges);
-- src:15839 | (d) documents of any other description specified in regulations made by the Secretary of State.
@ref s 1105(2) The documents to which the section applies (src:15835-15839)
GIVEN description IS A `s 1105(2) description of document`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1105(2) the section applies to the document` MEANS
    CONSIDER description
    WHEN `s 1105(2)(a) an agreement required to be forwarded to the registrar under Chapter 3 of Part 3 (agreements affecting the company's constitution)` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 1105(2)(b) a document required to be delivered under section 400(2)(e) or section 401(2)(f) (company included in accounts of larger group: copy of group accounts)` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 1105(2)(c) a certified copy delivered under Part 25 (company charges)` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 1105(2)(d) a document of any other description specified in regulations made by the Secretary of State` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 1105(2) another document` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the regulations under paragraph (d) may specify other descriptions and are not in the sources

-- src:15834 | (1) Documents to which this section applies may be drawn up and delivered to the registrar in a language other than English, but when delivered to the registrar they must be accompanied by a certified translation into English.
@ref s 1105(1) Documents to which the section applies may be delivered in another language with a certified translation (src:15834)
GIVEN `the section applies to the document` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1105(1) the document may be drawn up and delivered in a language other than English` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the section applies to the document`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
    OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Documents to which this section applies"

@ref s 1105(1) The delivery meets the requirement of a certified translation into English (src:15834)
GIVEN `the section applies to the document` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the document is delivered in a language other than English` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the document is accompanied by a certified translation into English` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1105(1) the delivery meets the requirement of s 1105(1)` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the section applies to the document`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
        IF (NOT `the document is delivered in a language other than English`)
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "but when delivered to the registrar they must be accompanied by a certified translation" speaks of a document delivered in another language
        ELSE IF `the document is accompanied by a certified translation into English`
             THEN JUST TRUE
             ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "when delivered to the registrar they must be accompanied by a certified translation into English"
    OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Documents to which this section applies"

-- ---- s 1106 ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:15842 | (1) A company may deliver to the registrar one or more certified translations of any document relating to the company that is or has been delivered to the registrar.
-- src:15843 | (2) The Secretary of State may by regulations specify—
-- src:15844 | (a) the languages, and
-- src:15845 | (b) the descriptions of document,
-- src:15846 | in relation to which this facility is available.
@ref s 1106(1) A company may deliver certified translations of any document relating to it (src:15842-15846)
GIVEN `the document relates to the company and is or has been delivered to the registrar` IS A BOOLEAN
      `regulations under subsection (2) make the facility available for the language and description of document` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1106(1) the company may deliver certified translations of the document` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the document relates to the company and is or has been delivered to the registrar`)
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any document relating to the company that is or has been delivered to the registrar"
    ELSE CONSIDER `regulations under subsection (2) make the facility available for the language and description of document`
         WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the facility is available only in relation to the languages and descriptions of document the regulations specify, and the text does not say the company may not deliver others
         WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the regulations under subsection (2) are not in the sources

-- (3): the regulations must provide that the facility is available as from 1 January 2007 in relation to all the official
-- languages of the European Union and all documents subject to the Directive disclosure requirements (section 1078).
-- src:15847 | (3) The regulations must provide that it is available as from 1st January 2007—
-- src:15848 | (a) in relation to all the official languages of the European Union, and
-- src:15849 | (b) in relation to all documents subject to the Directive disclosure requirements (see section 1078).
@ref s 1106(3) The regulations must make the facility available from 1 January 2007 (src:15847-15849)
GIVEN `the date` IS A DATE
      `the language is one of the official languages of the European Union` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the document is subject to the Directive disclosure requirements (see section 1078)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1106(3) the regulations must provide that the facility is available` MEANS
    IF `the date` AT LEAST (Date 1 1 2007) AND (`the language is one of the official languages of the European Union` OR `the document is subject to the Directive disclosure requirements (see section 1078)`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The regulations must provide that it is available as from 1st January 2007— (a) in relation to all the official languages of the European Union, and (b) in relation to all documents subject to the Directive disclosure requirements"

DECLARE `s 1106(4) requirement the registrar may impose` IS ONE OF
    `s 1106(4) the identification of the original document`
    `s 1106(4) the delivery of the translation in a form and manner enabling it to be associated with the original`
    `s 1106(4) some other requirement as to form and manner of delivery`

-- src:15850 | (4) The power of the registrar to impose requirements as to the form and manner of delivery includes power to impose requirements as to the identification of the original document and the delivery of the translation in a form and manner enabling it to be associated with the original.
@ref s 1106(4) The registrar's power to impose requirements as to form and manner (src:15850)
GIVEN requirement IS A `s 1106(4) requirement the registrar may impose`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1106(4) the power of the registrar to impose requirements includes power to impose the requirement` MEANS
    CONSIDER requirement
    WHEN `s 1106(4) the identification of the original document` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 1106(4) the delivery of the translation in a form and manner enabling it to be associated with the original` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 1106(4) some other requirement as to form and manner of delivery` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "includes power to impose requirements as to the identification of the original document and the delivery of the translation"

-- src:15852 | (6) This section does not apply where the original document was delivered to the registrar before this section came into force.
@ref s 1106(6) This section does not apply where the original was delivered before it came into force (src:15852)
GIVEN `the original document was delivered to the registrar before this section came into force` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1106(6) section 1106 applies` MEANS
    IF `the original document was delivered to the registrar before this section came into force`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This section does not apply where the original document was delivered to the registrar before this section came into force"
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection says when the section does not apply and does not say when it does

