    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the company may not rely on the translation as against a third party"
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "In the case of any discrepancy between the original language version of a document and a certified translation"

@ref s 1107(2)(b) A third party may rely on the translation unless the company shows knowledge of the original (src:15857)
GIVEN `there is a discrepancy between the original language version of a document and a certified translation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company shows that the third party had knowledge of the original` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1107(2)(b) the third party may rely on the translation` MEANS
    IF (NOT `there is a discrepancy between the original language version of a document and a certified translation`)
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "In the case of any discrepancy between the original language version of a document and a certified translation"
    ELSE IF `the company shows that the third party had knowledge of the original`
         THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a third party may rely on the translation unless the company shows that the third party had knowledge of the original"
         ELSE JUST TRUE

-- src:15858 | (3) A “third party” means a person other than the company or the registrar.
@ref s 1107(3) "third party" (src:15858)
GIVEN `the person is the company` IS A BOOLEAN
